citeturn230view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({"ref_id":"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/product/documents/320/327/a9384pis.pdf","lineno":null}); Total lines: 42
L0@P0: S-(5’-Adenosyl)-L-homocysteine
L1@P0: Product Number A 9384
L2@P0: Storage Temperature -0 °C
L3@P0: Product Description
L4@P0: Molecular Formula: C14H20N6O5S
L5@P0: Molecular Weight: 384.4
L6@P0: CAS Number: 979-92-0
L7@P0: Extinction Coefficient: EmM = 15.4 (260 nm in water or
L8@P0: 0.1 M NaCl)1
L9@P0: S-Adenosyl-L-homocysteine is the product of
L10@P0: enzymatic transmethylation reactions involving
L11@P0: S-Adenosylmethionine (SAM). It may be reconverted
L12@P0: to SAM after cleavage into adenosine and
L13@P0: L-homocysteine, which is the substrate of
L14@P0: thetin-homocysteine S-methyltransferase (EC 2.1.1.3)
L15@P0: Precautions and Disclaimer
L16@P0: For Laboratory Use Only. Not for drug, household or
L17@P0: other uses.
L18@P0: Preparation Instructions
L19@P0: The product is soluble in water (1 mg/ml).
L20@P0: Storage/Stability
L21@P0: S-Adenosyl-homocysteine is slowly oxidized to the
L22@P0: sulfoxide as a solid and in solution, and is protected
L23@P0: from oxidation by thiodiglycol. It is hydrolyzed in acid
L24@P0: solution (0.1 M HCl, 100 °C over 90 minutes) forming
L25@P0: S-ribosylhomocysteine. S-Adenosyl-homocysteine is
L26@P0: not hydrolyzed in neutral or alkaline solutions (stable
L27@P0: in 0.1 M NaOH at 25 °C over 10 minutes), but
L28@P0: oxidation is more rapid in alkaline solution. Neutral
L29@P0: solutions containing thiodiglycol are stable for long
L30@P0: periods at 25 °C.2
L31@P0: References
L32@P0: 1. Shapiro, S. K., and Ehninger, D. J. Anal.
L33@P0: Biochem., 15(2), 323-333 (1966).
L34@P0: 2. Dawson, R.M.C., et al., Data Biochemical
L35@P0: Research, 3rd ed., p. 2-3., Oxford University
L36@P0: Press, New York, (1986).
L37@P0: MES/ 10/02
L38@P0: Sigma brand products are sold through Sigma-Aldrich, Inc.
L39@P0: Sigma-Aldrich, Inc. warrants that its products conform to the information contained in this and other Sigma-Aldrich publications. Purchaser
L40@P0: must determine the suitability of the product(s) for their particular use. Additional terms and conditions may apply. Please see reverse side of
